# Sovren mainnet (sovr-1) validator — docker-compose config.
#
# You normally do NOT edit this file by hand. Run ./configure.sh, which copies
# it to .env and fills in the per-operator values (external address, moniker).
# Everything in the OFFICIAL section below is pre-filled from the current
# release and is kept up to date automatically (scripts/update-release-values.sh
# on each release) — verify against sovr-networks/mainnet/joining.md if you like,
# but you should not need to change it.

# =============================================================================
# OFFICIAL — pre-filled from the current mainnet release. Do not edit by hand.
# =============================================================================

# --- Image ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The PUBLIC node image, pinned by the linux/amd64 digest of v0.27.1 (what the
# published release + its checksums.txt correspond to). The image is multi-arch,
# but the docs and BINARY_SHA256 track amd64 only — arm64 support (index digest
# sha256:57e23f85…, arm64 child sha256:73ebb230…) is tracked in sovr-networks#12.
# On an arm64 host, do not use this pin as-is.
SOVR_NODE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/sovrn-tech/sovrd:v0.27.1@sha256:479ff7ce30a85dc0562bdb3837d3d6418873846aca12697887df714229e39bcd

# --- Chain identity ---------------------------------------------------------
CHAIN_ID=sovr-1
MINIMUM_GAS_PRICES=0.001usovr

# --- Integrity (verified by the entrypoint on every start; fail-closed) -----
# sha256 of the published genesis.json (mainnet/genesis.sha256 in sovr-networks).
GENESIS_SHA256=04529695e7ccfe32fcf3bc8031c343056d27cbe4aa3b3046027e27065bb9a855
# sha256 of the `sovrd` binary in the image (the Release's checksums.txt entry).
BINARY_SHA256=d35269a20eab4af073e3bd2d42d1619ce47f84ee42c2c8a451837d863b65d38d

# --- Peering (official seeds) -----------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated <nodeid>@host:26656 list from mainnet/joining.md.
SEEDS=381af5e4d0d5e24af3bb4d506b06081399622d01@seed1.mainnet.sovrchain.net:32000,68d9058a5dd7062d72d917ae8f2a2e30101b5a74@seed2.mainnet.sovrchain.net:32001

# --- Snapshot restore (REQUIRED to bootstrap — see README §5) ---------------
# A fresh sovr-1 node CANNOT sync from genesis (the chain has had many on-chain
# upgrades; a single modern binary can't reproduce historical app hashes). You
# MUST bootstrap from a published, signed archive snapshot at a height AFTER the
# latest on-chain upgrade. configure.sh sets SNAPSHOT_RESTORE=true for you.
SNAPSHOT_RESTORE=true
# Official mainnet snapshot bucket + cosign PUBLIC key (keyed verify). The node
# reads $SNAPSHOT_BASEURL/$SNAPSHOT_NETWORK/archive/latest.json(.sig).
SNAPSHOT_BASEURL=https://svrn-chain-snapshots-mainnet.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/snapshots
SNAPSHOT_NETWORK=mainnet
SNAPSHOT_COSIGN_PUBKEY=MFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAEv6XtLWy4H3IhmiLMUXEbRCeWswmXS8Y3xuNHo96Bwt2TbZSnwxnn4sHbl1/2cTH+b85pb/zGRIfURBad2ZOpfA==

# =============================================================================
# YOURS — configure.sh fills these in (or set them yourself).
# =============================================================================

# --- This validator ---------------------------------------------------------
# Public display name for your validator. (configure.sh prompts for this.)
MONIKER=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_MONIKER
# OPTIONAL — how the network dials YOU on P2P. Leave BLANK for a NAT'd,
# outbound-only validator (it signs and earns fine without inbound). Set it only
# if you want inbound peers: your public IP/DNS or the LB/elastic IP in front of
# the node (configure.sh auto-detects and offers to set it).
EXTERNAL_ADDRESS=
# OPTIONAL — how the P2P port is published. Default (unset) accepts inbound on all
# interfaces. For outbound-only (no inbound), set 127.0.0.1:26656:26656.
P2P_PORT_PUBLISH=
# Optional; seeds are usually enough.
PERSISTENT_PEERS=
# Local file signer. Leave as-is unless you wire an external signer (tmkms/HSM).
SIGNER_MODE=file
KEYRING_BACKEND=file

# TWO DISTINCT RPC anchors (comma-separated) whose block_hash must agree with the
# signed snapshot; the restore FAILS CLOSED if they're equal. Both public anchors
# are pre-filled so it works out of the box. NOTE: rpc + rpc2 currently share a
# backend (rpc2 moves to a second datacenter later), so this isn't yet a fully
# *independent* cross-check — for maximum safety replace the second with your own
# already-synced node or a trusted third-party sovr-1 RPC.
SNAPSHOT_ANCHORS=https://rpc.sovrchain.net,https://rpc2.sovrchain.net

# --- Host paths / resources -------------------------------------------------
# Host directory that holds the persistent node home (chain data + keys).
HOST_SOVR_HOME=./data
CPU_LIMIT=4
GOGC=100
#
# ⚠️  MEMORY — sized per box, deliberately left UNSET here. GOMEMLIMIT MUST fit
# your box's physical RAM, or Go grows its heap past RAM and the kernel OOM-kills
# sovrd — which (on mainnet's tight downtime window) jails and slashes you. Do NOT
# copy fixed values onto a smaller box. configure.sh sizes both from detected RAM
# (GOMEMLIMIT ≈ 75% of RAM, MEMORY_LIMIT ≈ 85% of RAM) and writes them into .env.
# If you set them by hand, follow this table — and add swap on a small box:
#     RAM     GOMEMLIMIT   MEMORY_LIMIT
#     2 GiB   1200MiB      1600m      (below the recommended minimum; add swap)
#     4 GiB   3000MiB      3600m
#     8 GiB   6500MiB      7600m
# Left blank on purpose: compose REQUIRES GOMEMLIMIT and will tell you to run
# configure.sh, so a verbatim copy can't silently over-commit a small box.
# GOMEMLIMIT=
# MEMORY_LIMIT=
